## own hint
✗ GitHub rejected the token
  Try: run `chitragit auth login github` again

## usage
✗ expected 1 argument(s), got 0
  Try: add --help to the command to see its arguments and flags

## plain
✗ something odd happened
  Try: run it again with --verbose; if it keeps failing, report it at https://github.com/TTox-Tech/ChitraGit/issues

## wrapped
✗ the disk is full
  Try: free some disk space and run the command again

## network
✗ a network error
  Try: check your network connection and run the command again

## auth
✗ a auth error
  Try: run `chitragit auth status` to see your logins, then `chitragit auth login <host>`

## not_found
✗ a not_found error
  Try: check the name or URL; `chitragit ls` lists the repos in this archive

## rate_limited
✗ a rate_limited error
  Try: wait a few minutes, or log in with `chitragit auth login` for a higher limit

## timeout
✗ a timeout error
  Try: run it again; for very large repos raise the limit with `chitragit config set sync.timeout 30m`

## unsafe_state
✗ a unsafe_state error
  Try: run `chitragit doctor` to see what is in the way

## conflict
✗ a conflict error
  Try: run `chitragit conflicts` to see and resolve it

## corrupt
✗ a corrupt error
  Try: run `chitragit doctor` to check the archive

## disk
✗ a disk error
  Try: free some disk space and run the command again

## permission
✗ a permission error
  Try: check that you can read and write this folder

## config
✗ a config error
  Try: run `chitragit config validate` to see which setting is wrong

## environment
✗ a environment error
  Try: run `chitragit doctor` to check git and your setup

## internal
✗ a internal error
  Try: run it again with --verbose; if it keeps failing, report it at https://github.com/TTox-Tech/ChitraGit/issues

